boojum@u.washington.edu (The Vanishing Valor) writes:

>BTW, FOR THOSE OF YOU WHO WANT TO LOSE INTRINSICS:  POTION OF LOSE INTRINSIC.

>Intrinsics gained from experience or from wearing an object could
>not be lost (neither could alaignment or luck....).

>Blessed: asks you what intrinsics (up to 4) you want to lose.
>Uncursed: lose one of your choice.
>Cursed: asks what intrinsic you want to lose, and removes EVERY OTHER ONE that 
>it can.

I'd say this is too strong. I'd prefer the following effects:

B: Lose one intrinsic of your choice. You must chose one, or the game
will pick one for you.
U: Lose one intrinsic. The game will always pick for you.
C: Removes all intrinsics.

Since the effects are to be permanent, I think it should be a scroll,
although there are also potions which confer permanent things, like
gain level.

There is one string attached: how would you choose WHICH ability would
be removed? You couldn't have the player just pick from a menu, since
the potion would then function as a potion of enlightenment as well...
Would this require another input-parser as wishing? This would be
tedious to program. Of course, you could do it via a menu that only
lists those innate abilities that you could actually lose, not your
alignment or abilities conferred by, for example, rings or amulets.

And I think that dipping a unicorn horn into one of these potions
should NOT clear them, since they can be useful in some cases. Also,
when hurled at monsters, they should NOT remove abilities, since these
are natural abilities.

